Food appraisal will notify you if food is already known to be rotten
(such as the partially eaten food ration).

It will also inform you (with the same message) if a corpse is old
enough to have a chance at causing "mild sickness" (1-8 damage) but
not old enough to cause food poisoning.

This may explain the inconsistency you are seeing.

Interestingly, food appraisal *will* kick in when you attempt to
resume eating the rotten food which just made you pass out, even
though (due to a bug, see my reply to Chris Randle) that food won't
actually cause you negative effects.


